# Design system

Before UI edits, read [`DESIGN.md`](DESIGN.md). Tokens live in `src/lib/styles/tokens.css` — do not invent colors, spacing, or fonts.

## Must

- Background `--paper`; panels `--surface` + `1px solid var(--line)` + `--radius-panel`
- Controls/buttons `--radius-control`; status/tags/toggles `--radius-round`; record face `--radius-record`
- Spacing only `--space-1`…`--space-7`; touch targets `--touch-min`
- Type via `--font-mono` and `--text-*`; labels uppercase + `--text-label`
- `--signal` only for record / clip / destructive / critical failure / idle trim boundary markers / Local File status chips / Collection upload-chip **failed** fill (fade grips use `--ink` wedges; active trim drag uses `--brand`)
- `--brand` / `--brand-soft` for primary CTA faces (`PrimaryButton`), action-toast border/fill, active waveform selection, active trim drag, **and** Collection `UploadStatusChip` queued/uploaded faces (neon blue-green; not record/destructive)
- Collection take rows use `UploadStatusChip` (morphing Local / Queued / Busy / Uploaded / Failed) — not a remounted `StatusLabel` swap
- Take play/pause uses `PlaybackControl` (smaller Record-style well; `--ink` face, not `--signal`)
- Discarded (outside-trim) waveform regions use `--disabled` wash + peaks; retained peaks stay `--ink`; peak-normalize preview gain uses one display scale across retained and discarded
- Reuse `$lib/ui` components; keep state as text + color (busy chip may be spinner-only with `aria-label`; phase copy lives in the upload sheet)
- Label `/collection` as Collection, groups as Field Sessions, and existing take metadata/details as Field Notes
- **Collect** is the take primary for retained trim → Local File; Collection **Upload** is a brand-well primary CTA with confirm→progress sheet
- Collection may use catalog rhythm, indexing, and compact deterministic marks derived from persisted take/source facts (neon fill from `--specimen-neon-*`)

## Must not

- Dark-first, purple gradients, glow, glass, pill clusters, card dashboards
- Hardcoded `#hex` / arbitrary px spacing / second typefaces (Inter, Roboto, etc.)
- Decorative or fake waveforms
- Drop shadows by default; floating marketing cards instead of structural panels
- Rarity, XP, streaks, collectible cards, celebratory Collection motion, or cloud implications
- Specimen marks that resemble waveforms or imply fingerprints/quality scores

Product depth: `briefing/03_VISUAL_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`. Waveforms: `.cursor/rules/waveform-ui.mdc`.
